<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43933" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">servātrix</span></b> , īcis,
			f.
		servator. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>She that keeps</i> or <i>preserves</i>, <i>a</i> (female) <i>savior</i>, <i>deliverer</i>, <i><span class="en">Ter. Hec.
				5, 4, 16</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sui,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fin. 5, 9, 26</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">servatrix celebrabere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					7, 50</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cohortis Inachiae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 5, 672</span></i>
			.—As <i>an epithet of goddesses</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Gud. 31, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">52,
			5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Inscr. Fabr. 470, 109</span></i> and
			110: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pectoris,</span>”
				<i>protectress</i>, <i>guardian</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 12, 606</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> With an abstr. object, <i>an observer</i>,
				<i>fulfiller</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">convenientiae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Doctr. Plat. p. 15, 32</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
